== globals ==
globals (v0, gated by default)
Definition: Names declared by package-level var in non-test files that hold mutable state, excluding _. In Go, sentinel errors (errors.New or fmt.Errorf of constants), //go:embed variables and boolean, numeric or string variables with a constant initializer or none that the package never assigns, increments or takes the address of (build information set by -ldflags), compiled regexps of constants, and read-only literal tables of constants that nothing writes an element of or passes to a call that could mutate them are left out. Generated files, those with a "Code generated ... DO NOT EDIT." header, are left out: a rebuild regenerates them; see tokens_est_generated.
Evidence: Hidden state: no direct study; plausible and kept at low weight.
Thresholds in the loaded config: none
